<title>FRANCE: Basle-Mulhouse tops French regional airports Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Basle-Mulhouse tops French regional airports Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's top ten regional airports</p>
<p>for flown airfreight in January-May 1997, with percentage change</p>
<p>on Jan-May 96 were:</p>
<p>				     TONNES	  PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>     1. Basle-Mulhouse*	17,542	 DOWN  10.0</p>
<p>     2. Marseille		16,880	 DOWN   7.3</p>
<p>     3. Lille**		  10,870	 UP    14.0</p>
<p>     4. Toulouse		 10,425	 UNCHANGED</p>
<p>     5. Lyon-Satolas	    9,795	 UP    11.6</p>
<p>     6. Nice***		   7,244	 UP     1.5</p>
<p>     7. Montpellier	     4,458	 UP   132.4</p>
<p>     8. Bordeaux		  2,682	 DOWN  18.0</p>
<p>     9. Strasbourg		2,013	 DOWN  30.8</p>
<p>    10. Rennes		    1,759	 UP    47.7</p>
<p>    *   includes traffic  handled in Swiss zone of airport.</p>
<p>**  also includes trucked air freight.</p>
<p>*** provisional figures.</p>
<p>The figures do not include France's major gateways for airfreight, Paris' CDG and Orly. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
